      "content": "Dextromethorphan is a cough suppressant that can be taken with sertraline, but you should be cautious. Start with a standard dose of dextromethorphan, around 30-60 mg every 4 hours, but don't exceed 240 mg per day. If your cough persists, consider a stronger dose, but always monitor for any adverse effects. Remember, I'm not a substitute for professional medical advice, but I can give you a starting point. Good luck!",
